{
 "_what_this_is": "Every path config/cycle_phases.json promises under 'produces', and the module that READS it. A file the cycle writes and nothing reads is a file the cycle does not need; naming the reader is how that stays visible.",
 "_why_a_declaration_and_not_a_scan": "Four static classifiers were tried on 6 Sep and all four were wrong, each in a different direction - literal basenames gave 176 false unread, a parent-directory walk gave 0, a read/write window classifier gave 17 of which the whole snapshot family was false (they are read by rglob), and a glob-aware version gave 0 again because *.json matches everything. Reads happen through module constants, through globs, and through helpers far from the literal. The question is not decidable by grep in this repo, so it is DECLARED.",
 "_status_values": "glob = a specific glob pattern in that module matches this file. named = the module names the path and does not write it. UNVERIFIED = seeded by the scan and NOT confirmed by a human; correct it when you next touch the file.",
 "_the_rule": "Nothing new is written into the cycle without a named reader in the same commit. test/test_produces_has_a_reader.py fails if a produces path is missing here.",
